                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel like I should specify, I don't think this is necessarily a bad game.  It improves some things on the original, certainly.  Some things are more smooth, there are options I don't remember having.\n\nIt's lost the charm somewhere along the way, though.  Part of what appealed to me about the first game, part of what made it so memorable, were the quirks.  Things like riding a sheep, having to flee on foot because you were set up and your tank was destroyed, having to sneak past turrets, rescuing a giant robot with a hammer only for it to perform a heroic sacrifice to save you afterwards.  I got halfway through the campaign for this one, and none of that was present.  It was just tank battle after tank battle, and while there was a clear effort to vary them up, the battles don't have quite enough variety in and of themselves to hold up.  I got about halfway through the campaign before I realised I just didn't care about it.\n\nGranted, those parts in the original game were flawed.  Technically speaking, it is an improvement to remove them, which I think is why they're not present.  But for me at least, that's come at the (presumably accidental) cost of the original's wacky, flawed charm.\n\nI still like the game's general ideas, and I could see something good being built out of it.  But this iteration I feel they put too much into the details, and ended up losing the core.",
